      "message": "We may have memory leak here. `message` already points to libspdm’s registered receiver buffer, with `*message_size` providing its capacity. Replacing it with `malloc()` leaks one allocation per received response because libspdm does not free replacement pointers. \nCan we retain the supplied pointer, verify that the payload fits, copy into  `*message`,and update `*message_size` to the actual payload length? A pointer into  `buf` would also be invalid because the caller’s vector is local.",
